play differently,

00:18:35.140 --> 00:18:36.820
Korean guys play differently.

00:18:36.820 --> 00:18:38.040
Everybody's differently.

00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:41.640
We have the kind
of in-game data,

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:46.150
I believe it's a really, really,
really powerful weapon for us.

00:18:49.307 --> 00:18:54.110
But problem is, we have a
huge legacy of our publishing

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:57.350
business from the PC side.

00:18:57.350 --> 00:19:00.590
So that is why we have a very
good relationship with Google

00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:01.570
Cloud.

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:08.120
And now, we hope to change
our legacy to a cloud trend

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:09.440
as soon as possible.

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:14.935
And we need huge help
from maybe Google PSO.

00:19:14.935 --> 00:19:15.715
[LAUGHS]

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:24.280
So because of the [INAUDIBLE]
transition from PC to mobile--

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:27.820
there are so many legacies
on the PC game side

00:19:27.820 --> 00:19:33.280
and the games [INAUDIBLE] last
year [INAUDIBLE] for cloud.

00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:37.910
And also, our analytics
is [INAUDIBLE] for mobile.

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:41.000
Are we are changing everything
as soon as possible.

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:46.600
And I think if we can
change our platform

00:19:46.600 --> 00:19:50.920
to a public cloud
like Google GCP,

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:55.120
and if we can combine everything
with the data we have,

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:59.350
I think we can be very strong
AI and machine learning company

00:19:59.350 --> 00:20:03.060
maybe, can be.

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:07.990
So Netmarble launched the
NARC earlier this year

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:11.920
to develop new business, new
AI business with this data

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:14.560
and our operation know-how.

00:20:14.560 --> 00:20:19.080
I know NARC means a little bit
drug-related thing in here.

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:22.790
But I said, I don't
use this name.

00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:26.380
But anyway, my chairman
decided to use this one.

00:20:26.380 --> 00:20:30.520
NARC means Netmarble
AI Revolution Center.

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:37.930
And revolution is our
key word for marketing.

00:20:37.930 --> 00:20:41.260
And we hire Juhnyoung Lee.

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:46.000
17 years-- he works at IBM
T.J. Watson Research Center.

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:52.660
And he is maybe one of
our fathers of Watson.

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:54.160
And everybody hate
Watson anyway.

00:20:56.890 --> 00:21:00.970
Juhnyoung Lee is currently
the head of NARC,

00:21:00.970 --> 00:21:05.410
and at the same time,
CTO of Netmarble.

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:11.670
He is leading every
change at technical side.

00:21:16.320 --> 00:21:18.910
Our industry [INAUDIBLE]
be very simple.

00:21:18.910 --> 00:21:25.080
We have to make game development
using an AI technique.

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:28.020
And we want to
make a more better

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:30.240
operation with AI solutions.

00:21:36.363 --> 00:21:38.930
Yes.

00:21:38.930 --> 00:21:42.352
This [INAUDIBLE] said,
we can do everything.

00:21:42.352 --> 00:21:44.290
We will do everything.

00:21:44.290 --> 00:21:49.950
But yeah, we already
make some progress

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.660
at reinforcement learning.

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:55.400
Everybody tried
that, but we tried

00:21:55.400 --> 00:22:00.430
reinforcement learning to
solve our balancing problems.

00:22:00.430 --> 00:22:08.230
And also, we are making a game
simulator to use AI technique.

00:22:08.230 --> 00:22:14.530
And at the same time, we are
doing some big data analysis

00:22:14.530 --> 00:22:18.060
on Google Cloud platform
GCP with BigQuery

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:20.770
And they use our
action data, and they

00:22:20.770 --> 00:22:22.840
use our profile data, QA
automation system-- that

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:24.430
kind of thing we are doing now.

00:22:24.430 --> 00:22:28.130
I take charge of this
side, not this side.

00:22:33.962 --> 00:22:36.890
Yeah.

00:22:36.890 --> 00:22:40.340
As I said, I'm in charge
over game service AI--

00:22:40.340 --> 00:22:44.660
AI related to game operations,
all kinds of activity,

00:22:44.660 --> 00:22:46.330
not outside of a game.

00:22:46.330 --> 00:22:50.060
For example, marketing
and operation and also,

00:22:50.060 --> 00:22:53.760
big data analysis.

00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:58.200
Yes, so I make us
a simple strategy--

00:22:58.200 --> 00:22:58.800
just the ABC.

00:23:03.070 --> 00:23:08.160
I want to provide actionable
insight to everybody inside

00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:09.150
of Netmarble.

00:23:12.960 --> 00:23:14.790
I don't know.

00:23:14.790 --> 00:23:20.100
Many game studios try
to prediction, right,

00:23:20.100 --> 00:23:23.070
churn prediction, LTV
prediction, many things.

00:23:23.070 --> 00:23:29.040
But is that kind of thing
actually meaningful,

00:23:29.040 --> 00:23:31.890
is my question.

00:23:31.890 --> 00:23:37.190
For many years, we tried to
copy the Western company.

00:23:37.190 --> 00:23:43.350
The Western company looks
like higher than our ability.

00:23:43.350 --> 00:23:46.060
So we tried to
catch up everything.

00:23:46.060 --> 00:23:49.170
So we try to predict churn.

00:23:49.170 --> 00:23:51.660
We tried to predict the LTV.

00:23:51.660 --> 00:23:57.780
And our conclusion is, yes,
we can do that, but so what?

00:23:57.780 --> 00:24:04.680
So what we can do to make more
money or make a better service

00:24:04.680 --> 00:24:06.280
is not the question.

00:24:06.280 --> 00:24:10.260
So these days, our
team is focusing

00:24:10.260 --> 00:24:12.300
on making actionable insight--

00:24:12.300 --> 00:24:18.030
deliver actionable insight to
everybody inside of Netmarble.

00:24:18.030 --> 00:24:23.040
For example, we give sort
of a simple loss prediction

00:24:23.040 --> 00:24:25.120
reporterd to the marketer.

00:24:25.120 --> 00:24:28.150
You can decide
everything based on data,

00:24:28.150 --> 00:24:33.180
and the marketer can decide--

00:24:33.180 --> 00:24:40.560
more money I will spend, or
stop spending, or changing

00:24:40.560 --> 00:24:41.520
a marketing channel.

00:24:41.520 --> 00:24:46.800
And every day, they are
trying to optimize everything

00:24:46.800 --> 00:24:47.780
based on data.

00:24:47.780 --> 00:24:50.710
That kind of thing, I
really want to do that.

00:24:50.710 --> 00:24:53.350
And business impact.

00:24:53.350 --> 00:24:56.460
AI and machine learning is
a very, very trendy tech,

00:24:56.460 --> 00:24:59.170
and it can solve many problems.

00:24:59.170 --> 00:25:08.190
But for me, solving technical
problems is not attractive.

00:25:08.190 --> 00:25:11.280
We really want to
solve simple problems,

00:25:11.280 --> 00:25:15.040
but that has a huge
business impact.

00:25:15.040 --> 00:25:19.690
For example, we develop the
ad fraud detecting system.

00:25:19.690 --> 00:25:22.590
That will save huge money
for performance marketing.

00:25:22.590 --> 00:25:25.650
And that kind of thing,
I really want to do that.

00:25:25.650 --> 00:25:29.820
At the same time, Netmarble
is a mobile game company.

00:25:29.820 --> 00:25:33.090
That means we don't have
very good developers,

00:25:33.090 --> 00:25:39.150
strong development tower
over AI or machine learning.

00:25:39.150 --> 00:25:43.590
To solve that problem, we
really tried collaboration

00:25:43.590 --> 00:25:45.150
with the other big companies.

00:25:45.150 --> 00:25:48.510
For example, we have a
very good relationship

00:25:48.510 --> 00:25:51.810
with Google Cloud-- a PSO team.

00:25:51.810 --> 00:25:54.330
PSO team provided
many insights to us

00:25:54.330 --> 00:26:01.860
to give develop a new system
and solve our headache problems.

00:26:01.860 --> 00:26:08.540
They are very smart, and we
are catching up their ability.

00:26:08.540 --> 00:26:16.955
But one more thing is, we
tried to solve right problem.

00:26:22.230 --> 00:26:28.030
The right problem is something
we really want to solve.

00:26:28.030 --> 00:26:34.320
And that is, human can
solve, but sometimes need

00:26:34.320 --> 00:26:38.700
a lot of people and it
takes a lot of time.

00:26:38.700 --> 00:26:42.150
That kind of problem
is perfect, perfect

00:26:42.150 --> 00:26:45.530
for using machine
learning, we believe.

00:26:45.530 --> 00:26:48.520
And we already
tried several cases

00:26:48.520 --> 00:26:52.490
and make ourself a
[INAUDIBLE] chart.

00:26:52.490 --> 00:26:58.820
So cases-- for marketing,
we do LTV prediction,

00:26:58.820 --> 00:27:04.230
ROAS prediction, and ad
fraud detection system.

00:27:04.230 --> 00:27:10.310
And as I said, we
developed LTV prediction,

00:27:10.310 --> 00:27:15.410
but nobody is using that
because it's a little bit

00:27:15.410 --> 00:27:18.170
hard to use for mass marketing.

00:27:18.170 --> 00:27:21.470
And in Korea, LTV
is not so important.

00:27:21.470 --> 00:27:26.630
And that is also the same in
Southeast Asia and maybe Japan.

00:27:26.630 --> 00:27:29.870
So we developed ROAS prediction.

00:27:29.870 --> 00:27:33.920
And we can recoup our
marketing budget--

00:27:36.630 --> 00:27:38.180
monthly base.

00:27:38.180 --> 00:27:40.400
We predict our
marketing budget will

00:27:40.400 --> 00:27:43.970
be [? liquid ?] in two months
or three months later or four

00:27:43.970 --> 00:27:45.240
months later.

00:27:45.240 --> 00:27:47.220
And then, we
developed the system.

00:27:47.220 --> 00:27:52.370
And the [INAUDIBLE]
is very, very high.

00:27:52.370 --> 00:27:57.430
Currently, it's--
how can I say--

00:27:57.430 --> 00:27:59.870
maybe plus or minus 15 days.

00:27:59.870 --> 00:28:02.040
It's really, really accurate.

00:28:02.040 --> 00:28:06.530
And our boss always
decide to spend more money

00:28:06.530 --> 00:28:08.990
based on a loss prediction.

00:28:08.990 --> 00:28:13.640
And also, we developed ad
fraud detection system.

00:28:13.640 --> 00:28:17.540
That is a headache
for many marketers.

00:28:17.540 --> 00:28:19.620
And it's really, really--

00:28:19.620 --> 00:28:21.350
there are so many solutions.

00:28:21.350 --> 00:28:24.570
For example, [INAUDIBLE] also
provides that kind of thing.

00:28:24.570 --> 00:28:26.750
And many [? trending ?]
companies

00:28:26.750 --> 00:28:31.430
provide some solution
to detect ad fraud.

00:28:31.430 --> 00:28:36.260
Problem is, we don't want to
rely on outside of the company.

00:28:36.260 --> 00:28:41.210
And we believe we have
plenty of data to detect

00:28:41.210 --> 00:28:43.115
ad fraud by ourselves.

00:28:43.115 --> 00:28:46.025
And we tried and we're
making huge success.

00:28:50.420 --> 00:28:56.240
For game service operation,
we developed churn report,

00:28:56.240 --> 00:28:59.760
like every other guys.

00:28:59.760 --> 00:29:02.870
But we use machine
learning to find out

00:29:02.870 --> 00:29:06.290
the difference between
leaving or staying.

00:29:06.290 --> 00:29:09.730
You just find what kind
of difference they have.

00:29:12.464 --> 00:29:20.320
Somebody leaving after
enjoying some [? PVP ?] loss.

00:29:20.320 --> 00:29:25.610
And somebody staying longer if
they played five or six times

00:29:25.610 --> 00:29:26.450
a day.

00:29:26.450 --> 00:29:31.180
That kind of insight we
want to extract from data.

00:29:31.180 --> 00:29:38.270
And every morning, our operation
team members get a report--

00:29:38.270 --> 00:29:41.780
what kind of trend is going on
and what kind of key difference

00:29:41.780 --> 00:29:45.590
between a churn [INAUDIBLE]
and staying [INAUDIBLE]..

00:29:45.590 --> 00:29:50.645
And also, we developed a
special churn prediction report.

00:29:53.970 --> 00:30:02.590
We are focusing on giving
us some clue for action.

00:30:02.590 --> 00:30:06.690
For example, yeah,
here's somebody,

00:30:06.690 --> 00:30:13.670
and their churn probability
is maybe over 90%.

00:30:13.670 --> 00:30:16.130
That means we can't do anything.

00:30:16.130 --> 00:30:20.090
He will go out, and he
will enjoy the other title.

00:30:20.090 --> 00:30:24.470
And somebody here in
the churn prediction

00:30:24.470 --> 00:30:29.160
will maybe a churn
rate, maybe 60% or 80%.

00:30:29.160 --> 00:30:33.370
But our second day
retention is over 50%.

00:30:33.370 --> 00:30:35.510
So 60% is higher or not?

00:30:35.510 --> 00:30:41.180
It's really, really hard to
understand for daily operation

00:30:41.180 --> 00:30:41.900
guides.

00:30:41.900 --> 00:30:45.900
So we just give ourselves
a simple guideline.

00:30:45.900 --> 00:30:54.880
Just focusing on this guy and
if you can hold this guy maybe

00:30:54.880 --> 00:30:59.470
the day after tomorrow, you
can get some huge retention

00:30:59.470 --> 00:31:03.110
in [? three ?] [? months. ?]
That kind of report,

00:31:03.110 --> 00:31:05.600
we deliver every day.

00:31:05.600 --> 00:31:10.340
And also, we develop
in-game anomaly detection.

00:31:10.340 --> 00:31:14.520
And then, that is our
collaboration project

00:31:14.520 --> 00:31:16.520
with Google PSO team.

00:31:21.370 --> 00:31:25.300
This day, our title
service period

00:31:25.300 --> 00:31:27.220
is longer longer and longer.

00:31:27.220 --> 00:31:30.590
That means, content
is very, very complex.

00:31:30.590 --> 00:31:34.830
It is really hard to
maintain bug free status.

00:31:34.830 --> 00:31:37.520
There will always be a bug.

00:31:37.520 --> 00:31:40.450
That means there is
always bug [INAUDIBLE]..

00:31:40.450 --> 00:31:44.480
How to find that kind of
user as soon as possible?

00:31:44.480 --> 00:31:50.200
That is one of the
most important problem

00:31:50.200 --> 00:31:53.480
to service a longer
and longer and longer.

00:31:53.480 --> 00:31:56.380
So we developed test systems.

00:31:56.380 --> 00:32:02.760
So I want to deep
dive three cases.

00:32:02.760 --> 00:32:05.630
One is Resemara Report.

00:32:05.630 --> 00:32:07.870
Do you know Resemara?

00:32:07.870 --> 00:32:09.610
That one you know, right?

00:32:09.610 --> 00:32:10.930
Yeah, you are from Japan?

00:32:10.930 --> 00:32:11.990
AUDIENCE: [INAUDIBLE]

00:32:11.990 --> 00:32:13.820
SPEAKER: Yes.

00:32:13.820 --> 00:32:17.810
Resemara is a very,
very interesting way

00:32:17.810 --> 00:32:21.850
to enjoy game content.

00:32:21.850 --> 00:32:27.476
Resemara is, reset,
combine, marathon.

00:32:27.476 --> 00:32:34.040
In Japan and in
Asia, usually, free

00:32:34.040 --> 00:32:38.360
to play game adopting
[INAUDIBLE] business model.

00:32:38.360 --> 00:32:41.960
[INAUDIBLE] means,
how can I say it?

00:32:41.960 --> 00:32:44.780
[INAUDIBLE] yeah, are you
familiar to [INAUDIBLE]??

00:32:44.780 --> 00:32:47.440
Something like a
lock box, right?

00:32:47.440 --> 00:32:54.250
And in Japan, marketing prices
are really, really high.

00:32:54.250 --> 00:33:01.170
That means, we want to hold the
user at least one hour a day.

00:33:01.170 --> 00:33:05.380
That means, we had to give
sort of a very good impression

00:33:05.380 --> 00:33:06.980
at the launching time.

00:33:06.980 --> 00:33:10.550
So we prepared some special
[INAUDIBLE] box only

00:33:10.550 --> 00:33:12.530
for new users.

00:33:12.530 --> 00:33:15.050
It contains something
like a very special card,

00:33:15.050 --> 00:33:18.920
or a very special character,
or a very special gift.

00:33:18.920 --> 00:33:24.540
To get that, user
reset, that means

00:33:24.540 --> 00:33:30.230
delete the app and reinstall
app continuously for maybe two

00:33:30.230 --> 00:33:32.800
or three days without stopping.

00:33:32.800 --> 00:33:36.410
Usually, maybe 200
times or 300 times, user

00:33:36.410 --> 00:33:39.350
can get actually what they want.

00:33:39.350 --> 00:33:43.880
For some time, it's over
1,000 or 2000 times.

00:33:43.880 --> 00:33:47.750
It looks very stupid, but
anyway, they tried that.

00:33:47.750 --> 00:33:51.650
And that is also one
of the main methods

00:33:51.650 --> 00:33:55.070
to enjoy the game in Japan
and in Southeast Asia.

00:33:58.310 --> 00:34:03.360
Problem is, can't
trust every KPI.

00:34:03.360 --> 00:34:04.980
Retention is a very low.

00:34:04.980 --> 00:34:07.170
That is because of Resemara.

00:34:07.170 --> 00:34:08.610
Nobody knows that.

00:34:08.610 --> 00:34:13.900
And first, a sign-up
gift is good enough.

00:34:13.900 --> 00:34:15.179
Nobody knows that.

00:34:15.179 --> 00:34:17.790
But something like
Resemara is too high.

00:34:17.790 --> 00:34:24.239
That means we give too good gift
to a [? sign ?] [? user. ?] But

00:34:24.239 --> 00:34:26.280
if the Resemara is
too small number,

00:34:26.280 --> 00:34:31.980
that means it's not good enough.

00:34:36.040 --> 00:34:38.690
And how many account
transitions happened?

00:34:38.690 --> 00:34:41.440
That is also a very
important thing.

00:34:41.440 --> 00:34:44.120
Something like this
title is very good,

00:34:44.120 --> 00:34:48.520
and this title gives us a
very special sign-up gift.

00:34:48.520 --> 00:34:50.550
And then, they do a Resemara.

00:34:50.550 --> 00:34:54.570
And there are some in China,
at this kind of situation,

00:34:54.570 --> 00:34:57.160
they make a Resemara
[? pump ?] to get

00:34:57.160 --> 00:34:58.990
themself a special account.

00:34:58.990 --> 00:35:03.100
And then, generating so
many accounts and sell that

00:35:03.100 --> 00:35:06.960
to Japan actual player.

00:35:06.960 --> 00:35:11.890
And that kind of thing can
break the balance of the game.

00:35:11.890 --> 00:35:15.050
So it's a very, very
dangerous thing.

00:35:15.050 --> 00:35:22.480
So we make Resemara report
system using many Google Cloud

00:35:22.480 --> 00:35:25.180
Platform services.

00:35:25.180 --> 00:35:28.130
We are not using machine
learning or some special thing.

00:35:28.130 --> 00:35:45.730
But anyway, you can analyze
every user local data

00:35:45.730 --> 00:35:48.310
in real time,
because of BigQuery

00:35:48.310 --> 00:35:51.220
and the powerful
Google Cloud platform.

00:35:51.220 --> 00:36:01.210
So finally, we can generate a
trustful KPI without Resemara.

00:36:01.210 --> 00:36:03.150
This is very important.

00:36:03.150 --> 00:36:08.110
We developed a thing
maybe last week--

00:36:08.110 --> 00:36:11.830
that is, I pushed my
developers to prepare "King

00:36:11.830 --> 00:36:14.463
of Fighter Allstar" launching.

00:36:19.049 --> 00:36:19.715
Ad fraud system.

00:36:22.710 --> 00:36:29.910
To explain how ad fraud
is a headache for me,

00:36:29.910 --> 00:36:36.450
I just searched Google and
found some very simple articles

00:36:36.450 --> 00:36:37.050
about that.

00:36:39.690 --> 00:36:42.790
Mobile ad spending is growing
another 20% this year.

00:36:47.900 --> 00:36:54.380
And 20% [INAUDIBLE].

00:36:54.380 --> 00:36:56.750
Every title has ad fraud.

00:36:56.750 --> 00:36:59.120
That means the illegal
downloads or something

00:36:59.120 --> 00:37:03.080
like a clicking [? palm ?] or
something like [INAUDIBLE],,

00:37:03.080 --> 00:37:07.550
just to get money without
installing, or stealing

00:37:07.550 --> 00:37:09.574
installs from others.

00:37:09.574 --> 00:37:11.990
That kind of thing is happening
again and again and again.

00:37:18.640 --> 00:37:20.195
This makes a large problem.

00:37:23.400 --> 00:37:26.310
That means they will
not enjoy our title,

00:37:26.310 --> 00:37:30.380
and that we spend money, and
that their retention will

00:37:30.380 --> 00:37:32.090
be going down.

00:37:32.090 --> 00:37:36.290
Problem is, without ad
fraud, actual retention

00:37:36.290 --> 00:37:38.750
will be a little more higher.

00:37:38.750 --> 00:37:43.880
